/-!
# Axiom audit for the standard charge-orbit bridge

This reusable audit separates the following statements:

* the concrete standard `U(5) -> SU(6)` subgroup and its full diagonal torus;
* restriction of actual and finite virtual trace characters to that subgroup;
* charge resolution in an arbitrary additive Abelian group, including finite
  groups where distinct integer lifts must be summed;
* the standard charge-orbit bridge-to-Abelian proton-operator neutrality proton-functional conclusion, which does not use anomaly
  cancellation;
* finite continuous-unitary `SU(6)` sources with independent Abelian source
  offsets and an affine central-degree charge, including finite charge groups.
* decomposition of an actual commuting unitary Abelian action into full
  character eigenspaces which are continuous-unitary `SU(6)`
  subrepresentations and reconstruct the original source.
* factorization of a gauge-twisted physical action into its standard central
  gauge part and an `SU(6)`-commuting Abelian action;
* raw ambient-weight charge resolution for a general color/weak block lift,
  with projection performed before normalization and finite-charge collisions
  summed by `Finsupp.mapDomain`;
* corrected physical charge-profile equalities and the resulting standard charge-orbit bridge-to-Abelian proton-operator neutrality
  theorem for actual common-gauge sources, including finite Abelian groups;
* actual trace realization of the raw block projection in standard diagonal
  coordinates, and transport to supplied physical actions conditional on one
  explicit fixed semisimple embedding classification standardizing conjugator;
* continuity of the factorized action and its sector characters, including
  integer charge classification for a residual circle;
* agreement between affine charge evaluation and the original physical
  action on the actual hypercharge character rigidity Laurent weight basis.
* faithful evaluation of charge-resolved characters on the product of the
  physical compact torus and an arbitrary Abelian residual group;
* the actual fifteen-weight SM target, with arbitrary charge-resolved gauge
  singlets, and recovery of the standard charge-orbit bridge spectrum, charge equalities, and Abelian proton-operator neutrality
  conclusion from whole-character equivalence, including the finite-Abelian
  specialization.
* construction of the source-side product-group representation on the actual
  charge-sector vector spaces, equality of its trace with the resolved
  evaluator, and agreement of its residual action with the supplied
  gauge-twisted physical action.
* equivalence of a local coefficient-level SM-only chiral-spectrum certificate
  with the canonical resolved target, and derivation of actual character
  equivalence and the standard charge-orbit bridge-to-Abelian proton-operator neutrality conclusion from that certificate.
* concrete `qque` and `duql` four-fermion signatures, their integral Standard
  Model and Lorentz quantum-number checks, nonzero determinant epsilon
  tensors, and identification of their residual characters with the two Abelian proton-operator neutrality
  functionals;
* construction of a supported invariant local-operator witness, which refutes
  exact prohibition by an ordinary Abelian charge selection rule without any
  nonzero-channel premise, including for finite Abelian groups;
* the logically separate conditional corollary: if at least one
  gauge-mediated channel is physically present, triviality of both operator
  characters prevents the symmetry from forbidding every present channel.

The audit deliberately does not derive the homomorphic gauge lift, local
coefficient spectrum, or a nonzero channel-presence proposition from every
gauge-theory model.  The local-operator result is an EFT operator-class
statement and carries no Wilson coefficient.
-/

